    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n70870" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νίπτρον</span></b> , τό, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νίζω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>water for washing,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				10.78
			</span></i>: mostly in pl., <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				225
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ion</u>
				1174
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Hel.</u>
				1384
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				12.68
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Mel.
			</span></i>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παῖδες ν. ἔδοσαν κατὰ χειρῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Philox.
					2.39
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Νίπτρα, τά,</span> the <i>Bath Scene,</i> title of play by
			Sophocles on the recognition of Odysseus by his nurse; also applied
			to <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				19
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Po.</u>
				1460a26
			</span></i>, and to the <i>Bath Scene</i> in that book, ib.<i><span class="en">
				1454b30
			</span></i>.</div>
